From 59767c8e05439b6a0f0a7ad8d8c5c5b98d407fa2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+openwrt@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [PATCH 2/8] wifi: mt76: mt7915: do not let the TX backoff subtraction

 underflow

mt7915_mcu_get_chan_mib_info() subtracts the accumulated TXOP backoff
from the TX duration to get the channel busy time. Both operands are
u64 and nothing bounds backoff by the duration. The MIB counters wrap,
so after a wrap the backoff can exceed the duration and the subtraction
wraps to a value near 2^64. The delta guard does not catch it: the
wrapped result is larger than the previous sample, so it is accepted as
a large forward step and permanently corrupts the survey busy time.

Clamp the subtraction. This is complementary to the mt7915_mib_delta()
guard, which rejects a counter that stepped backwards.

Signed-off-by: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+openwrt@gmail.com>
---
 mt7915/mcu.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/mt7915/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7915/mcu.c
@@ -3272,8 +3272,14 @@ int mt7915_mcu_get_chan_mib_info(struct
 #define __res_u64(s) le64_to_cpu(res[s].data)
 	/* subtract Tx backoff time from Tx duration for MT7915 */
 	if (is_mt7915(&dev->mt76)) {
+		u64 tx = __res_u64(1);
 		u64 backoff = (__res_u64(4) & 0xffff) * 79;  /* 16us + 9us * 7 */
-		cc_tx = __res_u64(1) - backoff;
+
+		/* the MIB counters wrap, and a wrapped backoff value can
+		 * exceed the TX duration. Do not let this u64 subtraction
+		 * underflow, the result would be stored as a huge delta.
+		 */
+		cc_tx = backoff < tx ? tx - backoff : 0;
 	} else {
 		cc_tx = __res_u64(1);
 	}
